  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"terminal#20269\", \"terminal#19383\", \"terminal#17246\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before, and I found no fix or workaround in the archive. Your fault offset 0x2c924 on 1.24.2605.12001 is the same one reported in terminal#20269. That ticket is a crash on 1.24.11321.0 in AtlasEngine::PaintCursor on the render thread, with an access violation reading a null pointer at about 0xC0. The user there also ran Claude Code tabs. terminal#19383 is the same PaintCursor failure bucket, hit while drag-merging two windows on 1.22, and a later comment says it also reproduced on a newer build. terminal#17246 is the older drag-merge crash. Its first fix, #17251, covered only part of the problem, and the ticket is not a match for your exact signature. Your crash is most likely the PaintCursor bug in the Atlas renderer, with the drag-merge acting as the trigger, rather than a regression of #17246. Add your details to terminal#20269 and terminal#19383: the build, the offset, the drag-merge trigger, and the heavy-scrollback and RADAR_PRE_LEAK context. Share the dump through a private channel, such as a Feedback Hub upload, and not as a public attachment, because it contains scrollback. Until it's fixed, avoid dragging tabs between windows while heavy output is streaming. Instead, open a new tab in the target window.\"}",
